                            // ************           Instance vs Model Based Machine learning             ************

// Instance Based 

Here model checks the similarity score of its nearest negihbours to classify its position , therefore we need to maintained trained data so new point will use its nearest 
points in the trained data to cassify itself ex: KNN ... etc.

// model Based

Here model uses trained data to derive a equation and therefore divides according to equation and whenever a new point comes it uses equation and reaches its desired point based on
equation and here we need not maintain the trained data and we can throw it because new data always goes according to equation ex: linear regression ... etc.



                          // ************            Machine Learning Life Cycle Developement            **************


it has several steps :

Step 1: Frame the problem : You have to Understand what the problem is, So once you get a clarity then you need not to change the developement process because you found a new issue, so its 
always suggested to cleary understand and define the problem before reaching the solution.

Step 2: Data Gathering: Once the problem is framed, you have to gather the data so you can continue next steps, there are diffrent ways to gather the data ex: CSV files,
web scraping, online datsets ... etc.

Step 3: Data Preprocessing: Once you got the data, you have to clean the data becuase they will have too many duplicates, null values and nosiy data, so to use the best data you
have to preprocess which means clean the data so good that you will get the best possible output.

Step 4: Exploratory Data Analysis: Once you pre-process the Data you have to understand the data to the next level which will help you to simplify next steps for you, like you have to 
understand coloumns and analysis what each data is expressing and you can perform univariate, bivariate, multivariate analysis so you will have a better understanding about the data.
It is said to invest most time here so we can build an exceptional model.

Step 5: Feature Engineering: After Analysing the Data, this step becomes easy, here we use those coloumns and create a new coloumn based on our requirement, or in other words we modify 
data according to the model or requirement.

Step 6: Model Building: Here we use the data to build model and predict or classify values as per the problem statement.  We can use multiple known models and combine them to make
an extremly powerfull Model as per our requirement

Step 7: Model Evaluation: Once Model is Built we evalute its performance, efficiecy and other metrics using diffrent metric methods.

Step 8: Testing : Once Evaluted we test them in production environment.

Step 9: Optimize : Based on Testing results and FeedBacks we optimize the model.

Step 10: Deployment: Finally we deploy the model for all the customers.



