Tensor = structured collection of numbers arranged along one or more axes.

* Tensor = a way to store numbers in multiple dimensions.
* It is an extension of scalars, vectors, and matrices.

Type      Dimension   Example
Scalar    0D          5
Vector    1D          [1, 2, 3]
Matrix    2D          [[1,2], [3,4]]
Tensor    3D+         Multiple matrices stacked together

Important terms:
